[6]  what opens and closes a fenced code block: at least three backticks or tildes, up to three spaces of indentation, a closing fence of the same character with at least as many of them; an unclosed fence runs to the end of the containing block; the content is literal text 
[7]  §4.5 Fenced code blocks (text copy `.ufo/waves/round-50/c2/commonmark-0.31.2-s4.5.txt`) 
[8]  "A code fence is a sequence of at least three consecutive backtick characters or tildes." — so a section scanner must not treat a `## ` line inside a fence as a heading 
